-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Pac-Mania
  Publisher   Grandslam, 1988
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Pac-Mania (1988)(Grandslam)(128K).z80
  MD5         e9cb908bc86661ff81732665741393cc

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Pac-Man yellow with a red mouth; the ghosts red, cyan for the
              ghost that jumps with Pac-Man and orange in their third look;
              frightened ghosts blue, flashing blue and red; eyes white;
              fruit, tokens and scores in the Spec256 conversion's colours.
              The maze and panel are the game's own. Source: Enhanced colours
              from the MVV package's older Spec256 conversion, painter not
              established, with Pac-Man and the ghosts repainted for Jon
              Attree.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: first release: the 128K release with AY music, every figure
              a sprite, R and CPU speed restored by every hook, whole Sinclair
              ROM image for NextZXOS v2.10, five tested cheats, the approved
              Enhanced colours as an option

  Note        The 128K release with AY music. The game starts at once: its
              loading screen shows while the .nex loads, and no key is needed
              to leave it. Every moving figure is a Next sprite: Pac-Man
              bright yellow and the ghosts in the round's colour, as the
              original draws them, without the yellow clash around Pac-Man;
              the maze and panel keep the original's colours. Enhanced
              colours, off by default, is the look approved on 2026-11-03.
              With Start with 9 lives the panel still shows at most five
              faces, as the original does. Known issues: about 0.5% slower
              than the original in steady play in JNext (whole runs -0.4% to
              +1.0%). Missing: hardware testing; full natural completion of
              every round (the all-rounds test used a cheat); the archive's
              Lives (1-128) value prompt (fixed at 9 here); the 48K release is
              not a target.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Start with 9 lives
   2  Infinite lives
   3  Turbo speed
   4  Infinite credits
   5  Immunity

  The archive's POKEs for Pac-Mania (one .pok serves every release), each
  tested alone on this 128K release; Lives (1-128) is fixed at 9 and Turbo
  Pacman is named Turbo speed.

